WEBVTT

00:12.150 --> 00:14.820
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

00:15.660 --> 00:19.030
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
Super Cute Angels ♥

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Boom!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Super Adorable</b>

01:31.360 --> 01:32.810
Sayurin!

01:32.810 --> 01:34.240
Over here, over here!

01:32.900 --> 01:37.490
<b>Episode 8:
Yakiniku with Friends Is Super Delish</b>

01:32.900 --> 01:37.490
<b>Episode 8:
Yakiniku with Friends Is Super Delish</b>

01:34.240 --> 01:37.040
What's the big deal? Dragging 
me out here like this.

01:37.040 --> 01:40.710
Shh! There. See? Look at that.

01:40.710 --> 01:42.560
What is this anyway?

01:42.560 --> 01:43.120
Oh!

01:46.920 --> 01:49.300
H-Hey, is that...?

01:49.300 --> 01:50.050
Mm-hmm.

01:50.050 --> 01:51.850
Shiki and Natsukawa are—

01:50.820 --> 01:53.260
Rena-senpai is wearing a kimono!

01:53.600 --> 01:56.710
This is so rare! 
She looks super adorable in it!

01:56.710 --> 01:58.350
Is <i>that</i> what you noticed?

02:02.670 --> 02:06.650
They're both in kimonos 
dressed to match. It's totally—

02:06.650 --> 02:08.360
A date, right?

02:08.940 --> 02:11.070
Rena-senpai and Tsubasa.

02:13.520 --> 02:19.860
<b>Mom
Mii! Emergency!

Tsuba-chi is on a date
with another girl!
Kyaa! (>_<)</b>

02:14.270 --> 02:19.090
Mom sent me a message saying 
Tsubasa was out with some girl.

02:19.090 --> 02:24.050
I asked where, and when I found out it 
was Rena-senpai I was like, "oh, my god!"

02:24.050 --> 02:26.620
Yeah, but why did you call me?

02:26.620 --> 02:29.010
Huh? Hmm.

02:29.750 --> 02:31.050
Just because?

02:31.050 --> 02:32.410
You don't even know?

02:32.410 --> 02:35.950
Huh? I thought you'd be really interested!

02:35.950 --> 02:37.530
Well, I guess I am.

02:38.000 --> 02:41.060
All right, I might as well play along.

02:41.060 --> 02:42.390
That's my girl!

02:42.760 --> 02:44.190
Keep it down!

02:44.890 --> 02:46.980
Hey, we gotta get going!

02:52.610 --> 02:54.360
She's so pretty!

02:54.610 --> 02:57.440
<i>I've never been to a place like 
this wearing Japanese clothes.</i>

02:57.440 --> 03:01.040
<i>It's kind of a weird feeling.</i>

03:02.190 --> 03:04.060
Look at that, Shiki-kun!

03:04.120 --> 03:08.330
<b>Soran Bushi</b>

03:04.120 --> 03:08.330
<b>Herring
Love</b>

03:05.950 --> 03:08.330
Isn't he just the cutest?

03:08.330 --> 03:11.290
What is that thing? A bear?

03:11.290 --> 03:15.590
It's Melon Kuma-san! 
The local mascot for Yubari City.

03:15.590 --> 03:18.340
I simply adore this little guy!

03:18.550 --> 03:21.100
<i>I didn't realize she was 
into stuff like this.</i>

03:21.950 --> 03:25.100
There are so many other cuties, too.

03:25.380 --> 03:27.490
Aren't they just so adorable?

03:27.490 --> 03:28.510
<i>I don't know...</i>

03:28.510 --> 03:31.370
<i>They're weird, but I can kind of 
see myself warming up to them.</i>

03:32.050 --> 03:35.110
In that case, would you 
like me to win one for you?

03:35.110 --> 03:36.860
Huh? Would you mind?

03:37.230 --> 03:38.860
Please do!

03:41.740 --> 03:43.490
Aww, no good.

03:43.490 --> 03:47.330
That was close. Let's try one 
more time. Just one more!

03:47.330 --> 03:47.920
Sure.

03:47.920 --> 03:49.090
Good luck!

03:49.090 --> 03:51.040
I'll get 'em this time!

03:51.040 --> 03:55.270
Not just head-on, dummy! You gotta view 
from the side to assess the depth, too!

03:55.270 --> 03:56.960
Everyone knows that!

03:56.960 --> 03:59.090
Aww, no luck again.

03:59.810 --> 04:02.030
I can't take this. I have to 
go show them how it's done!

04:02.030 --> 04:04.120
Sayurin, calm down! Calm down!

04:04.120 --> 04:05.740
But I can't just stand by and wat—

04:04.870 --> 04:06.490
Oh! I got one!

04:09.690 --> 04:10.790
What is that?

04:10.790 --> 04:12.210
Wonderful!

04:12.210 --> 04:16.280
This little fellow is Kitami City's 
local mascot. His name is Mint-kun!

04:16.280 --> 04:19.700
Well, he is now my present to you, Senpai.

04:19.700 --> 04:22.150
I'm sorry I couldn't get the bear, though.

04:22.150 --> 04:26.370
Do you mean it? 
Thank you very much! I'm so happy!

04:28.190 --> 04:30.190
I promise to you that...

04:30.590 --> 04:32.880
I will forever take care of Mint-kun!

04:32.880 --> 04:34.760
<i>Th-That's...</i>

04:34.760 --> 04:36.420
<i>God-tier purity!</i>

04:36.420 --> 04:40.990
I-If it makes you that happy, 
then I'm very glad I won it.

04:41.380 --> 04:43.760
Tsubasa is really kind, isn't he?

04:43.760 --> 04:47.510
He for real tries to do his best 
for anyone, no matter who it is.

04:47.510 --> 04:50.310
I really respect that, you know?

04:50.310 --> 04:53.770
Even now with Rena-senpai, 
it's for real. I can tell!

04:54.190 --> 04:59.610
He's living in a new place, with people he 
doesn't know. That's gotta be hard on him.

04:59.880 --> 05:02.320
But he doesn't show it at all.

05:02.320 --> 05:04.580
Instead, I see him trying 
twice as hard as anyone else.

05:05.370 --> 05:08.170
You could say he's, like, 
the coolest guy around.

05:09.400 --> 05:14.060
I wish... I could be more like that, too.

05:17.460 --> 05:20.230
I-I mean, I guess that's probably 
what people think, right?

05:20.230 --> 05:22.470
Um, so what do you think, Sayurin?

05:23.850 --> 05:25.200
Wait, really?

05:25.530 --> 05:26.610
Oh, my bad.

05:26.090 --> 05:27.570


05:26.610 --> 05:29.690
I had to give it a shot after 
watching them. You said something?

05:29.690 --> 05:30.390
Huh?!

05:31.990 --> 05:35.660
It's almost time for that 
movie you wanted to see.

05:36.630 --> 05:39.920
You're right. I was having 
so much fun, I almost forgot.

05:40.500 --> 05:43.710
The cinema is on the fourth floor. 
Shall we go?

05:44.550 --> 05:46.910
Come on, Sayurin! We have to go now!

05:46.910 --> 05:50.280
Hold on. I need some bags 
for the stuff I won.

05:50.280 --> 05:51.870
Sayurin!

05:55.410 --> 05:58.540
Aww! Tsubasa and Senpai already left!

05:58.540 --> 06:00.930
I'll give you half of my winnings, 
so don't be mad, okay?

06:00.930 --> 06:01.800
Really?

06:02.120 --> 06:04.410
Hooray! Thank you!

06:04.410 --> 06:05.800
You're so easy, lol.

06:07.330 --> 06:10.120
It sounded like they were going to a movie.

06:10.120 --> 06:12.850
There's actually an anime movie 
out that I wanted to see.

06:12.850 --> 06:15.550
Oh? M'kay, why don't we go see that?

06:15.550 --> 06:17.400
Seriously? Thanks!

06:17.710 --> 06:20.050
I'm looking forward to the film!

06:20.050 --> 06:20.930
Yeah.

06:20.930 --> 06:23.900
<i>The purity radiates from her body like light!</i>

06:45.470 --> 06:49.320
It's all about someone struggling 
to establish her career.

06:49.320 --> 06:50.870
Seems like Senpai.

06:58.620 --> 06:59.920
Understood.

07:01.690 --> 07:05.450
What do I have to do to prove myself? 
To finally earn their honest praise?

07:06.350 --> 07:11.070
Will I always have to measure myself 
against other people's expectations?

07:13.190 --> 07:15.520
<i>Uh, I feel so sorry for her.</i>

07:15.520 --> 07:18.080
<i>But I bet she'll start to 
turn everything around now.</i>

07:23.070 --> 07:26.100
Is Senpai... crying?

07:30.410 --> 07:31.970
That was really good, wasn't it?

07:32.380 --> 07:36.390
That scene at the end when she picks herself 
up and is finally recognized by everyone

07:36.390 --> 07:39.640
worldwide gave me such a good feeling. 
I thought it was really moving!

07:39.640 --> 07:43.360
I started crying halfway through the movie!

07:45.280 --> 07:48.090
Do you cry very easily, Senpai?

07:48.090 --> 07:50.850
Oh, no! This is very unusual for me.

07:51.460 --> 07:56.680
But I really felt like I identified 
with the film's lead character.

07:57.600 --> 08:03.250
I also study very hard, I take lessons, 
but even when I do well,

08:03.250 --> 08:05.670
I rarely get much praise.

08:05.670 --> 08:08.590
Huh? So it's the same for you?

08:08.590 --> 08:09.710
The same for me?

08:09.710 --> 08:14.470
Ah, I mean... I didn't know even people 
like you dealt with that kind of stuff.

08:14.840 --> 08:15.680
Oh?

08:16.640 --> 08:19.560
I went through the same thing for a while.

08:19.560 --> 08:23.440
It ended in a fight with my parents, 
and I basically ran away here to Hokkaido.

08:23.440 --> 08:24.830
You fought?

08:25.190 --> 08:29.160
Shiki-kun, are you actually... 
an aggressive person?

08:29.160 --> 08:29.810
Huh?

08:30.130 --> 08:32.650
No, no, I don't think so.

08:32.650 --> 08:36.200
But maybe I can be a little 
stubborn sometimes.

08:36.960 --> 08:39.230
Oh. I see.

08:40.970 --> 08:43.880
I'm probably the opposite of that.

08:44.910 --> 08:45.800
The opposite?

08:46.570 --> 08:50.180
I'm always very conscious 
of how others see me.

08:47.670 --> 08:50.180
<b>Certificate
 Highest Honors to
 Natsukawa Rena
 for Excellence in Calligraphy</b>

08:51.750 --> 08:54.090
I feel that if I don't keep 
getting better and better,

08:54.090 --> 08:56.430
then nobody will appreciate me.

08:54.600 --> 08:57.270
<b>Every Day a Blessing</b>

09:00.210 --> 09:03.390
So sometimes I wonder, 
what in the world am I doing here?

09:04.310 --> 09:08.130
If nobody appreciated me, 
would I just stop entirely?

09:09.490 --> 09:14.490
If so, then I wonder... do I even matter?

09:17.920 --> 09:22.550
But if that's what inspires you 
to succeed, Natsukawa-senpai,

09:22.550 --> 09:24.590
doesn't it also have a positive side?

09:25.570 --> 09:30.260
You work so hard to earn praise. 
I think everyone knows what that feels like.

09:30.650 --> 09:35.510
But I don't think many people take it 
seriously and actually finish what they start.

09:35.830 --> 09:36.630
Well, I'm not—

09:36.630 --> 09:41.100
I bet a lot of people see you and think, 
"I should try to become my best self, too!"

09:43.100 --> 09:45.350
People... see me?

09:45.350 --> 09:46.170
Yes!

09:46.540 --> 09:51.090
I don't mean to make this about me, 
but I know what you mean when you say

09:51.090 --> 09:52.790
you aren't sure if you matter.

09:53.100 --> 09:56.180
Of course, I'm sure it was a 
lot harder for you, though.

09:56.910 --> 10:00.500
Anyway, remember the scene when 
the lead shouted, "I am who I am"?

10:00.490 --> 10:07.460
I am who I am...

10:00.490 --> 10:07.460
I will be myself

10:01.390 --> 10:04.450
She realized she couldn't be anybody 
but herself. But not in a negative way,

10:04.450 --> 10:07.460
a positive one. Wasn't that a great part?

10:09.550 --> 10:12.340
Yes. That was my favorite scene.

10:12.660 --> 10:13.930
Mine, too.

10:17.430 --> 10:21.620
I suppose we do have some... 
things in common, don't we?

10:21.620 --> 10:23.690
Our circumstances, our troubles and such.

10:24.050 --> 10:26.110
And we are next-door neighbors.

10:26.110 --> 10:30.690
Definitely. And isn't it unusual 
that we both own our own kimonos?

10:31.050 --> 10:35.260
You know, many people think that I'm strange

10:35.260 --> 10:38.780
and I rarely feel that 
people truly understand me.

10:38.780 --> 10:40.950
So I'm very happy to have met you, Shiki-kun!

10:42.780 --> 10:47.190
Uh, I'm really happy that 
I met you, too, Senpai!

10:47.190 --> 10:49.820
After spending the day together 
and talking and stuff,

10:49.820 --> 10:52.590
I want to know even more about you!

10:55.500 --> 10:56.840
Shiki-kun, do...

10:58.650 --> 11:01.310
you have a girlfriend or anything?

11:03.390 --> 11:04.310
Huh?!

11:05.850 --> 11:09.490
I know you're a responsible person, 
Shiki-kun, so if you did have a girlfriend,

11:09.490 --> 11:12.650
I doubt you'd be out on a date with me.

11:16.860 --> 11:20.030
That was great! That director is a god!

11:21.270 --> 11:22.050
Huh?!

11:25.740 --> 11:27.880
No, I don't.

11:27.880 --> 11:29.850
Don't you ever get lonely?

11:29.850 --> 11:30.500
Huh?

11:30.500 --> 11:33.580
I mean, you just came to Hokkaido 
and didn't know anybody

11:33.580 --> 11:38.430
so you had to make all new friends. 
Wasn't that difficult for you?

11:39.260 --> 11:42.620
If I was in your place, 
I would be very lonely.

11:43.990 --> 11:47.360
You're right. A lot of things 
have been difficult for me here.

11:48.440 --> 11:50.610
But now, and I know this might sound weird,

11:50.870 --> 11:52.730
but I've made some very special friends here

11:53.180 --> 11:57.550
who truly accept me for who I am. 
So I'm not lonely at all!

12:00.980 --> 12:03.230
I also have a senpai who works very hard

12:03.230 --> 12:05.450
and is a shining example 
for everyone around her.

12:05.970 --> 12:08.090
Every day I spend in Hokkaido, 
the people around me

12:08.090 --> 12:10.460
give me the strength to keep going!

12:14.410 --> 12:18.810
I'm very pleased that you are enjoying 
Hokkaido, Shiki-kun. That's a relief to hear.

12:18.810 --> 12:22.160
I am! Next time, why don't 
we all hang out together?

12:22.160 --> 12:23.900
Oh? Would that be all right?

12:23.900 --> 12:24.810
Of course!

12:24.810 --> 12:26.220
I'm in!

12:27.410 --> 12:29.190
Fuyuki-san and Akino-san?!

12:29.190 --> 12:32.400
H-Hang on! Are you just gonna 
blow our cover like that?

12:32.670 --> 12:33.410
Cover?

12:33.410 --> 12:35.530
What? Were we undercover?

12:35.530 --> 12:36.860
Of course we were!

12:36.860 --> 12:38.410
You were undercover.

12:39.290 --> 12:41.670
Wait! No... were you guys listening to us?!

12:41.670 --> 12:44.030
The stuff about us all hanging out, right?

12:44.030 --> 12:45.670
But, Tsubasa, not fair!

12:45.670 --> 12:50.010
You can't go behind my back and take 
Rena-senpai on a date all by yourself!

12:50.010 --> 12:51.490
Be-Behind your back?

12:51.490 --> 12:53.650
I do apologize for the intrusion!

12:53.650 --> 12:55.380
And who might these ladies be?

12:55.380 --> 12:58.870
Uh, my classmates Fuyuki-san and Akino-san.

12:58.870 --> 13:00.670
The heck was that, Tsuba-cha?!

13:00.670 --> 13:04.090
This is when you're supposed to introduce 
us as your "important friends," right?!

13:04.090 --> 13:05.650
Are you... really?

13:05.650 --> 13:07.860
You want to be introduced as "important"?

13:07.860 --> 13:11.990
Oh come on, Sayurin! You're one of 
Tsuba-cha's important friends, too, aren't you?

13:11.990 --> 13:15.080
Huh?! Oh. Uh... okay.

13:15.080 --> 13:19.030
Well, I do think you are both 
important, but you know...

13:19.030 --> 13:20.660
But you know what, exactly?

13:20.660 --> 13:24.140
Uh, well, how do I...

13:21.990 --> 13:24.660
I see. I believe I understand now.

13:27.790 --> 13:29.620
Rena-senpai! Um...

13:30.040 --> 13:33.890
I'm in first-year, class 4. 
My name is Fuyuki Minami!

13:33.890 --> 13:35.620
This is the first time we've spoken,

13:35.620 --> 13:39.630
but I've actually really 
admired you for a long time.

13:39.630 --> 13:41.770
And so... how do I say this...

13:41.770 --> 13:44.090
I'm your fan! Please shake my hand!

13:44.090 --> 13:46.270
Huh? Y-You mean me?

13:46.270 --> 13:49.890
Y-Yes! I mean me! I mean, Rena-senpai!

13:49.890 --> 13:52.510
<i>I've never seen either of 
them this nervous before.</i>

14:03.980 --> 14:07.540
Your hands are so soft, so shapely, so light,

14:07.540 --> 14:10.750
everything to your fingertips 
is silky smooth!

14:11.030 --> 14:13.670
You're a goddess for real! Thank you so much!

14:13.670 --> 14:15.560
I will never wash my hands again!

14:15.560 --> 14:19.330
I'm very flattered, but you 
probably should wash your hands.

14:19.330 --> 14:23.800
If you say so, Senpai! I'll wash them 
a hundred times! A thousand times!

14:24.210 --> 14:27.770
Hey. Chill. You're freaking her out.

14:27.770 --> 14:31.180
Huh? Did I say something weird? Huh?

14:32.830 --> 14:35.090
Um, Rena-senpai...?

14:35.530 --> 14:38.160
Uh, I-I'm really sorry!

14:38.160 --> 14:40.860
Oh, no, this is actually quite fun.

14:41.770 --> 14:46.620
It is easy to see why Shiki-kun 
thinks you're both so important.

14:49.110 --> 14:52.460
Hey, you four over there!

14:54.090 --> 14:57.000
Hey, you four over there!

14:58.230 --> 14:59.630
Yoo-hoo!

14:59.850 --> 15:01.200
Mom?

15:01.200 --> 15:02.260
Good afternoon!

15:02.260 --> 15:05.940
Tsuba-chi, lookin' good! 
So are your lady friends.

15:05.940 --> 15:07.640
H-Hello.

15:07.640 --> 15:09.050
Pleased to meet you.

15:09.050 --> 15:10.420
Howdy, howdy!

15:10.420 --> 15:13.410
What's up, Mom? You're super cheery today.

15:13.410 --> 15:15.020
Actually...

15:15.020 --> 15:18.230
I sold a bunch of the clothes 
I put up on Merycari,

15:18.230 --> 15:20.770
so I got some bonus income!

15:20.770 --> 15:24.020
And I thought, since it looks 
like the gang's all here,

15:24.020 --> 15:26.800
do you all wanna go out to eat yakiniku?

15:26.800 --> 15:27.960
Yakiniku?!

15:27.960 --> 15:31.030
Um, but does that mean 
you're going to treat us?

15:31.030 --> 15:35.590
Kitami has the highest number of yakiniku 
restaurants per capita in all of Hokkaido!

15:35.590 --> 15:39.560
Yeah, it's like someone in Tokyo saying, 
"wanna get ramen?" Or maybe—

15:39.560 --> 15:41.710
"Wanna get cake?" Kinda like that?

15:41.710 --> 15:45.070
Cake and yakiniku is a super 
weird comparison, though.

15:45.070 --> 15:48.690
But it's all good! You don't need to be shy!

15:48.690 --> 15:49.300
Okay?

15:49.300 --> 15:50.900
O-Okay!

15:53.310 --> 15:55.800
<b>Kitami
Yakiniku</b>

15:53.310 --> 15:55.800
<b>Kitami
Yakiniku</b>

15:53.310 --> 15:55.800
<b>While others are delicious but costly,
 Marusho is delicious and inexpensive.
Marusho
Our staff can't wait to greet you with a smile!</b>

15:55.800 --> 15:57.310
Cheers!

15:57.310 --> 15:59.560
We're having a post-test party!

15:59.880 --> 16:01.750
Keep 'em grilling!

16:01.750 --> 16:03.190
It all looks so good!

16:03.190 --> 16:05.170
I'll take up position here.

16:05.960 --> 16:08.350
Your kimonos are probably going to smell.

16:08.350 --> 16:11.250
That's all right. My kimono is washable.

16:11.250 --> 16:15.750
Well, at least put the outer haori 
in a plastic bag. You, too, Tsuba-chi.

16:15.750 --> 16:17.270
Thank you very much.

16:18.540 --> 16:19.870
Thank you very much.

16:23.110 --> 16:24.750
First one!

16:25.090 --> 16:26.510
Huh? Is that even ready?

16:26.510 --> 16:29.510
I like it best kinda rare.

16:35.770 --> 16:37.680
Super delish!

16:38.120 --> 16:40.290
Amay-and-zing! Seriously!

16:40.290 --> 16:43.680
The juicy burst of short rib 
flavor is filling my mouth!

16:43.680 --> 16:48.470
The first bite is all firm, beefy texture, 
but then it starts melting in my mouth!

16:48.470 --> 16:51.130
I suppose my beef tongue 
should be about ready.

16:51.130 --> 16:53.620
The fatty pork is probably good to go.

16:56.200 --> 16:59.290
Mmm! Yum!

16:59.730 --> 17:04.670
A crispy surface texture combined 
with lusciously juicy insides!

17:04.670 --> 17:08.300
And crunchy green onions are 
a perfect topping for it!

17:08.600 --> 17:12.200
There's nothing as richly 
flavorful as pork fat!

17:12.200 --> 17:16.120
The savory aroma filling my 
mouth is almost overwhelming!

17:17.390 --> 17:18.910
It's so good!

17:18.910 --> 17:22.320
<i>They all make it sound so delicious!</i>

17:22.320 --> 17:24.770
Come on, come on. Eat up, Tsuba-chi!

17:24.770 --> 17:25.900
O-Okay!

17:25.900 --> 17:28.860
The hanger steak here is super good!

17:28.860 --> 17:31.070
Hanger steak? What kind of cut is that?

17:31.320 --> 17:33.790
Huh? You've never heard of it, Tsubasa?

17:33.790 --> 17:38.410
I believe that in Tokyo and elsewhere, 
it gets categorized as skirt steak.

17:38.410 --> 17:40.830
Oh. So what part is skirt steak?

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Beef Variety Meats

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Tongue

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Heart

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Hanger Steak

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Rumen

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Liver

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Large Intestine

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Tripe

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Skirt Steak

17:40.830 --> 17:47.840
Small Intestine

17:41.040 --> 17:43.990
It's from the diaphragm. 
It's a type of variety meat.

17:43.990 --> 17:47.840
Oh, no kidding. I always thought 
it was just normal beef.

17:48.510 --> 17:50.380
I'll help myself to some hanger steak.

17:54.650 --> 17:57.560
It isn't fatty at all, but it's super tender!

17:57.560 --> 18:01.230
And with such a thick cut, 
the succulent, meaty taste spills out

18:01.230 --> 18:03.440
with every delicious bite as 
if to cheer, "this is the one!"

18:03.940 --> 18:06.650
This is true Hokkaido yakiniku!

18:06.650 --> 18:09.030
It's too good! No...

18:09.030 --> 18:12.210
It's too super delish!

18:12.750 --> 18:14.060
Right?

18:14.060 --> 18:15.870
Help yourself! Eat up!

18:15.870 --> 18:17.030
All right!

18:17.370 --> 18:21.040
<i>If this is the quality you get 
for a casual yakiniku meal here,</i>

18:21.040 --> 18:23.050
<i>Hokkaido is incredible!</i>

18:23.050 --> 18:25.510
<i>This beef is so good!</i>

18:26.840 --> 18:29.170
When I heard people talk about Hokkaido meat,

18:29.170 --> 18:31.160
I always thought they 
meant lamb or Jingisukan.

18:31.160 --> 18:33.160
Do you eat that at restaurants often?

18:33.160 --> 18:36.850
Nah, we don't need to go 
to a restaurant for that.

18:36.850 --> 18:37.340
Huh?

18:37.340 --> 18:39.990
Jingisukan is something 
we usually eat at home.

18:39.990 --> 18:42.850
Same with my family. We eat it at home.

18:43.150 --> 18:46.000
So it is a common home dish, then?

18:46.000 --> 18:47.880
I always thought of it as 
more of a gourmet dish.

18:47.880 --> 18:50.070
Yeah, no way.

18:50.070 --> 18:52.860
We even have Jingisukan grills at home.

18:53.110 --> 18:55.250
Wow, even grills?

18:55.250 --> 18:58.210
Well, it's kind of like 
takoyaki grills in Osaka.

18:58.210 --> 19:01.930
Yeah! They say every home has to have one.

19:01.930 --> 19:05.450
You could make it on a regular 
hot plate, too, though.

19:05.450 --> 19:07.170
I feel so lucky...

19:08.000 --> 19:11.760
to be talking about lamb dishes 
with a mouth full of beef!

19:19.060 --> 19:21.450
You sure are a lucky guy, aren't you?

19:21.450 --> 19:22.440
What do you mean?

19:22.440 --> 19:24.570
Come on, Tsuba-chi.

19:24.570 --> 19:28.480
Sitting here surrounded by these adorable girls? 
You must be in heaven!

19:29.400 --> 19:34.150
I mean, check out Sayurin and Rena-chima. 
Aren't they both super adorbs?

19:35.030 --> 19:38.320
Hold on, Mom. 
Why'd you leave me out of that?

19:38.320 --> 19:40.950
Well, that's because you're family, Mii.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.600
Oh. And Rena-senpai might be 
in her own special category.

19:44.600 --> 19:47.630
You always get first place in 
your class for tests, don't you?

19:47.630 --> 19:49.710
First place? Really?

19:49.710 --> 19:51.520
Y-Yes, I suppose so.

19:51.520 --> 19:53.130
Amazing!

19:53.130 --> 19:56.090
Amaze... Wait, how did you know?

19:56.090 --> 19:57.630
'Cause I'm her fan!

19:57.840 --> 20:03.140
Wow, Senpai. That pretty <i>and</i> smart? 
Talk about winning the gene lottery.

20:03.370 --> 20:04.180
Oh...

20:05.040 --> 20:06.220
No, I simply—

20:06.220 --> 20:08.060
You got it all wrong, Sayurin.

20:08.060 --> 20:11.190
She works super hard! We just don't see it.

20:11.190 --> 20:14.570
I mean, look at her makeup and nails. 
That sort of stuff takes effort!

20:14.960 --> 20:18.730
And she gets first place because 
she studies like crazy!

20:19.190 --> 20:24.030
Whenever I see you, Rena-senpai, I think, 
"I'm wanna be my best self, too!"

20:26.450 --> 20:28.280
You're totally right, Fuyuki.

20:28.840 --> 20:31.850
I apologize, Senpai. 
That was extremely rude of me.

20:31.850 --> 20:33.880
Oh, no. It's all right!

20:33.880 --> 20:38.200
That one would've been perfect if 
you actually did study harder, Mii.

20:38.200 --> 20:39.090
Boo-hoo.

20:39.090 --> 20:40.390
Don't mind it, Fuyuki.

20:41.690 --> 20:42.610
Senpai.

20:44.980 --> 20:48.350
See? People really do 
appreciate your efforts.

20:51.450 --> 20:52.330
Thank you!

20:53.760 --> 20:56.900
Come on, come on, keep 'em coming!

20:57.920 --> 20:59.690
Thank you for the food!

20:59.690 --> 21:01.410
You are very welcome!

21:03.130 --> 21:06.040
Hey, hey, Tsubasa. Can I ask you something?

21:06.040 --> 21:06.810
Huh?

21:06.810 --> 21:09.500
Tsubasa, are you and Rena-senpai going out?

21:09.500 --> 21:12.780
Huh? No, no, no! Not a chance!

21:12.780 --> 21:14.260
Even though you went on a date?

21:14.260 --> 21:17.450
Yeah, well, there were 
various reasons for that.

21:17.450 --> 21:18.880
Hmm?

21:18.880 --> 21:20.380
Well, I guess we can call it even.

21:21.370 --> 21:23.550
If, in exchange, the next date...

21:24.410 --> 21:25.710
is my turn, okay?

21:25.710 --> 21:26.310
Huh?

21:27.150 --> 21:28.660
We could even spend the night.

21:28.660 --> 21:33.240
Wh-Wh-What are you talking about, 
Fuyuki-san? That's... no way!

21:33.240 --> 21:35.770
I'm just kidding! Kidding!

21:35.770 --> 21:37.860
You reacted so hard! Hilarious!

21:37.860 --> 21:40.160
<i>What an absolutely demonic joke!</i>

21:40.160 --> 21:41.700
Oh. But that part is real.

21:41.700 --> 21:45.330
We're going on a date! 
It's almost spring break!

21:46.990 --> 21:51.510
Hey, guys, listen up! 
When it gets warmer, wanna have a barbecue?

21:51.510 --> 21:54.260
We can make Jingisukan together!

21:54.260 --> 21:56.360
Will you come, too, Rena-senpai?

21:56.360 --> 21:58.510
Is it all right if I join?

21:58.510 --> 22:00.370
For sure, for sure!

22:00.370 --> 22:01.380
I will, then!

22:01.380 --> 22:02.840
You're coming, right Sayurin?

22:02.840 --> 22:05.360
Well, I do like Jingisukan.

22:05.360 --> 22:08.510
All right! Oh, man! It's gonna be great!

22:09.160 --> 22:10.600
Right, Tsuba-cha?

22:13.170 --> 22:14.090
Mm-hmm!

22:15.560 --> 22:16.480
<i>She's right.</i>

22:17.250 --> 22:18.610
<i>It's almost spring.</i>

22:19.110 --> 22:20.900
<i>Spring in Hokkaido...</i>

22:24.650 --> 22:27.490
<i>I'm so excited. I can't wait!</i>
